cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
title: >-
  OSR11: Compound Flooding Events in the South Atlantic Eastern Coast
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Danilo Couto
    family-names: de Souza
    email: danilo.oceano@usp.br
    affiliation: >-
      Institute of Astronomy, Geophysics and Atmospheric Sciences, University
      of Sao Paulo
  - given-names: Carolina Barnez
    family-names: Gramcianinov
  - given-names: Ricardo
    family-names: de Camargo
  - given-names: Karine Bastos
    family-names: Leal
    affiliation: National Institute for Space Research
abstract: >-
  This software identifies compound coastal flooding events along the Brazilian
  coast by combining tide-free sea-level extremes, significant-wave-height
  extremes, and an astronomical-tide level gate. It characterizes compound
  hazards from 1993 to 2025 and integrates hazard, population exposure, and
  social vulnerability to produce municipal coastal risk indices and identify
  priority hotspots for adaptation planning.
keywords:
  - compound flooding
  - coastal hazards
  - storm surge
  - ocean waves
  - coastal risk
  - social vulnerability
  - Brazil
repository-code: "https://github.com/daniloceano/osr11"
